[{"text":"DiracGamma[x, dim] is the head of all Dirac matrices and slashes (in the internal representation). Use GA, GAD, GS or GSD for manual (short) input.","anchor":"diracgamma"},{"text":"DiracGamma[x, 4] simplifies to DiracGamma[x].","anchor":"diracgamma"},{"text":"DiracGamma[5] is \\(\\gamma ^5\\).","anchor":"diracgamma"},{"text":"DiracGamma[6] is \\((1+\\gamma ^5)/2\\).","anchor":"diracgamma"},{"text":"DiracGamma[7] is \\((1-\\gamma ^5)/2\\).","anchor":"diracgamma"},{"text":"Overview, DiracGammaExpand, GA, DiracSimplify, GS, DiracTrick.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"DiracGamma[5]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^5\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[LorentzIndex[\\[Alpha]]]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\alpha }\\]","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"A Dirac-slash, i.e., \\(\\gamma ^{\\mu }q_{\\mu}\\), is displayed as \\(\\gamma \\cdot q\\).","anchor":"cb2-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[Momentum[q]]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[Momentum[q]] . DiracGamma[Momentum[p - q]]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb4-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[Momentum[q, D], D]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\gamma \\cdot q\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[p - q] . GS[p] DiracGammaExpand[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}-\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex = GAD[\\[Mu]] . GSD[p - q] . GSD[q] . GAD[\\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\gamma ^{\\mu }.(\\gamma \\cdot (p-q)).(\\gamma \\cdot q).\\gamma ^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracTrick[ex]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[4 ((p-q)\\cdot q)+(D-4) (\\gamma \\cdot (p-q)).(\\gamma \\cdot q)\\]","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[ex]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[D (\\gamma \\cdot p).(\\gamma \\cdot q)-D q^2-4 (\\gamma \\cdot p).(\\gamma \\cdot q)+4 (p\\cdot q)\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma may also carry Cartesian indices or appear contracted with Cartesian momenta.","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[CartesianIndex[i]]","anchor":"cb10","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\gamma }^i\\]","anchor":"cb10-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[CartesianIndex[i, D - 1], D]","anchor":"cb11","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\gamma ^i\\]","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGamma[CartesianMomentum[p]]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"}]